        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/2282f766-ad0d-4086-aae6-13afb4249e7d,1793391372185/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C285%2C5472%2C3078%29%3B' alt='An elephant and a man walking.' width='620' height='349' title='Zoo attendant one, Paul Williams walks with Lucy the elephant at the Edmonton Valley Zoo, in Edmonton on Tuesday March 21, 2023.'/><p>The federal government has effectively shelved a bill meant to phase out the captivity and import and export of elephants and great apes in Canada. Some animal advocates suspect it has to do with the government's current preoccupation with the tariff war and other economic issues.</p>",
