        "date_published": "2026-11-01T04:00:00+00:00",
        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/daf1c49f-29a8-416d-bfd0-2ec437c18ed8,1793367228359/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C1210%2C4160%2C2340%29%3B' alt='A person in a leather jacket poses in profile, looking over at the camera.' width='620' height='349' title='Asher'/><p>The recent success of high-profile 2SLGBTQ+ shows like Heated Rivalry may make it seem like Canada is providing a wealth of queer representation, but actors and experts tell CBC that complex trans stories are increasingly disappearing from screens as anti-trans rhetoric increases across the globe \u2014 warning that this only makes it harder to combat dehumanizing myths.</p>",
