        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-11-01T04:00:00+00:00",
        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/8039cb75-1956-4017-8fdd-960bd3e0d6c7,1793307301773/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C312%2C6000%2C3375%29%3B' alt='Five men dressed all in white are singing on a stage with blue lights shining down.' width='620' height='349' title='The Backstreet Boys perform onstage during at Little Caesars Arena in Detroit, Michigan in December 2022. They&apos;re currently doing a musical residency in Vegas, attracting millions of fans over their run. And in Toronto, they&apos;re hosting a 12-night residency in Toronto.'/><p>Attending a concert is no longer just a night out: with the rise of the music residency and select-city tours, artists are saving on travel costs, while fans have to shell out for what's being sold being as the trip of a lifetime.</p>",
