    {
        "age": null,
        "album": "",
        "author": "Angela Hennessy",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "comments": [],
        "date_created": "2026-11-01T19:58:48.077690+00:00",
        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-11-01T04:00:00+00:00",
        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/b7b155c7-49e2-42a7-a4aa-94bc8c6d2c0c,1793387704203/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C30%2C2000%2C1125%29%3B' alt='Donald Trump supporters wait at a rally.' width='620' height='349' title='Supporters try to get a view of then-Republican presidential candidate Donald Trump as he arrives at a campaign rally at Albuquerque International Sunport on Oct. 31, 2024, in Albuquerque, N.M.'/><p>Young men are increasingly turned off by U.S. President Donald Trump, and right-leaning podcasters are distancing themselves, too \u2014 a trend that experts say could swing House and potential Senate seats in next week's midterms.</p>",
